WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.485
Lab 2 runs the check on a real export,

2
00:00:02.485 --> 00:00:07.438
in a test tenant with Microsoft Entra
Connect or Cloud Sync configured.

3
00:00:07.438 --> 00:00:10.532
A Global Administrator
of the test tenant saves

4
00:00:10.532 --> 00:00:13.626
the response of the one
privileged read to a file.

5
00:00:13.626 --> 00:00:17.763
That's the only step that needs the
role; nothing in the kit runs with it.

6
00:00:17.763 --> 00:00:22.587
Then you run the check on that export as
any user, and compare the result with the

7
00:00:22.587 --> 00:00:27.412
export, line by line, so you know the check
reads the tenant's real response shape.

8
00:00:27.412 --> 00:00:32.001
To back it out, step four deletes the
export once the run's evidence is stored.

9
00:00:32.001 --> 00:00:36.297
The export isn't evidence by
itself; the run's manifest,

10
00:00:36.297 --> 00:00:39.325
with a hash for every file of the run, is.

11
00:00:39.325 --> 00:00:41.475
The authors haven't run Lab 2.

12
00:00:41.475 --> 00:00:45.020
Follow Chapter 03's Lab 2, step by step.
